{"title":"Spoke & Sprocket","sub":"A second bike shop: great summers, empty winters","type":"Investment / capacity","industry":"Consumer services","geo":"Netherlands","diff":1,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Seasonality · utilisation · payback","prompt":"Spoke & Sprocket runs a busy bicycle repair shop in Amsterdam. The owners want to open a second shop near the university in Utrecht, which would cost $150k to fit out. They want to know if it would pay off, and how to deal with the quiet winter months.","clarify":[{"q":"How seasonal is demand?","a":"Very: about 55 repairs a day from April to September, about 25 a day in winter."},{"q":"Staffing?","a":"Three technicians, needed to cope with summer. Each can do about 20 repairs a day."},{"q":"Pricing?","a":"Average repair $28; parts are 30% of that."},{"q":"Trading days?","a":"Assume about 300 a year: 150 from April to September and 150 from October to March."},{"q":"Objective?","a":"Payback within three years."}],"structure":{"root":"Will the Utrecht shop pay back within three years?","branches":[{"head":"Revenue","items":["Repairs per day by season","Average price","Trading days"]},{"head":"Costs","items":["Parts","Technicians (fixed)","Rent and other"]},{"head":"Using winter capacity","items":["Idle technician time","Ways to fill it"]}]},"hypothesis":"Summer is strong, but the shop pays for three technicians all year. Profit probably depends on filling winter capacity.","questions":[{"q":"Estimate annual profit and payback for the new shop.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"394.408156pt\" height=\"185.46pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 394.408156 185.46\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M -0 185.46 L 394.408156 185.46 L 394.408156 -0 L -0 -0 L -0 185.46 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"