m=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-5c\" d=\"M 582 0 Q 493 0 493 83 L 493 3309 Q 493 3392 563 3392 L 947 3392 Q 1018 3392 1018 3322 L 1018 2950 Q 1018 2918 1030 2912 Q 1043 2906 1075 2931 Q 1286 3098 1468 3216 Q 1651 3334 1843 3395 Q 2035 3456 2253 3456 Q 2752 3456 3017 3187 Q 3283 2918 3283 2490 L 3283 102 Q 3283 0 3187 0 L 2829 0 Q 2784 0 2765 22 Q 2746 45 2746 83 L 2746 2368 Q 2746 2682 2586 2858 Q 2426 3034 2080 3034 Q 1894 3034 1731 2973 Q 1568 2912 1401 2800 Q 1235 2688 1030 2515 L 1030 96 Q 1030 0 934 0 L 582 0 L 582 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-be\" d=\"M 166 4749 L 166 4749 L 384 4749 Q 454 4749 493 4698 Q 890 4096 1142 3360 Q 1395 2624 1395 1824 Q 1395 1280 1289 803 Q 1184 326 992 -115 Q 800 -557 538 -1011 Q 506 -1056 461 -1056 L 224 -1056 Q 186 -1056 176 -1033 Q 166 -1011 179 -992 Q 518 -269 691 412 Q 864 1094 864 1818 Q 864 2579 656 3321 Q 448 4064 128 4691 Q 115 4710 124 4729 Q 134 4749 166 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(70.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-66\" transform=\"translate(125.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(185.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-44\" transform=\"translate(240 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-50\" transform=\"translate(294.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6c\" transform=\"translate(318.109375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-75\" transform=\"translate(356.8125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a5\" transform=\"translate(409.8125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-bd\" transform=\"translate(431.21875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-83\" transform=\"translate(459.8125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a5\" transform=\"translate(523.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6c\" transform=\"translate(545.3125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-48\" transform=\"translate(582.71875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-44\" transform=\"translate(640.8125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-4f\" transform=\"translate(695.015625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-5c\" transform=\"translate(753.421875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-50\" transform=\"translate(811.828125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-44\" transform=\"translate(835.734375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-50\" transform=\"translate(889.9375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(913.84375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-5c\" transform=\"translate(968.640625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-6a\" transform=\"translate(1027.046875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-be\" transform=\"translate(1078.25 0)\"/></g></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p0eb921d91e\"><rect x=\"41.248156\" y=\"27.296\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"133.056\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Expected demand vs capacity","note":null},"answer":"<p>Repairs: 150 days × 55 + 150 days × 25 = <b>12,000</b>.</p> <p>Revenue: 12,000 × $28 = $336k. Contribution after parts (70%): $235k.</p> <p>Profit: $235k − $171k = <b>$64k a year</b>. Payback: $150k ÷ $64k = <b>2.3 years</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> it meets the three-year hurdle, but only just.</p>","note":"Fixed costs per year: rent $36k, technicians $120k, other $15k."},{"q":"In winter, how much technician time is idle? The owners are considering a student plan: $9 a month for two services a year. They expect 800 sign-ups, and each service uses about $6 of parts. What is it worth?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Winter idle capacity: 1 − 25 ÷ 60 = <b>58%</b>.</p> <p>Plan revenue: 800 × $9 × 12 = $86.4k. Services: 1,600 at about $6 of parts each = −$9.6k (labour is free: it uses idle winter time).</p> <p>Cannibalisation: if 40% of subscribers would have paid for about 1.5 repairs a year anyway: −$9.4k of lost margin.</p> <p>Net: <b>+$67.4k a year</b>, which would cut payback to about 1.1 years.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> worth it, as long as services are booked into winter. Let subscribers book only from October to March.</p>"},{"q":"What else could fill winter capacity?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Fleet contracts</b>: maintain bikes for delivery companies, hotels and bike-share operators</li> <li><b>Winter service</b> promotion: lights, brakes and tyres before the dark months</li> <li><b>Refurbish and sell used bikes</b> to students in September</li> <li><b>Flex staff</b>: a seasonal technician in summer instead of a third full-time one</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Open the Utrecht shop: it should make about $64k a year and pay back in 2.3 years, inside the three-year hurdle. Its weakness is winter, when 58% of technician time is idle. A student plan that books services into October to March adds about $67.4k a year and cuts payback to 1.1 years; fleet contracts could add more. Risk: a weak first summer while the shop builds awareness. Next step: talk to two local fleet operators before signing the lease.","great":["Builds revenue by season, not with one average","Measures idle capacity","Counts cannibalisation in the subscription maths","Uses idle time as a near-free resource"],"id":32,"slug":"spoke-sprocket"}